\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-225\li225\sl200\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1.\cf0  Eternal Ruler of the ceaseless round
\par \pard\li225\sl200\slmult0\qj Of  circling planets singing on their way,
\par Guide of the nations from the night profound
\par Into the glory of the perfect day:
\par Rule in our hearts, that we may ever be
\par Guided and strengthened and upheld by Thee.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl200\slmult0\qj\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2.  We are of Thee, the children of Thy love,
\par \pard\li225\sl200\slmult0\qj The brothers of Thy well-beloved Son
\par Descend, O Holy Spirit, like a dove,
\par Into our hearts, that we may be as one;
\par As one with Thee, to whom we ever tend;
\par As one with Him, our Brother and our Friend.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl200\slmult0\qj\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. We would be one in hatred of all wrong,
\par \pard\li225\sl200\slmult0\qj One in our love of all things sweet and fair,
\par One with the joy that breaketh into song,
\par One with the grief that trembleth into prayer,
\par One in the power that makes the children free
\par To follow truth, and thus to follow Thee.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl200\slmult0\qj\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4.  O clothe us with Thy heavenly armour, Lord,
\par \pard\li225\sl200\slmult0\qj Thy trusty shield, Thy sword of love divine;
\par Our inspiration be Thy constant word;
\par We ask no victories that are not Thine:
\par Give or withhold, let pain or pleasure be;
\par Enough to know that we are serving Thee.
\par \pard\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2\fs14 
\par }

